{
  "ai": {
    "chunks": [
      "The eminent and learned Shaykh Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn b. Musa b. Babawayh al-Qummi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. Abi Ishaq b. Ahmad al-Laythi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad b. al-Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Husayn Ali b. Muhammad b. Ali al-Mufti narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, from his father, from Yahya b. Ayyash, saying: Ali b. Asim narrated to us, saying: Abu Harun al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said:",
      "Indeed, Rajab is the month of Allah, the Deaf, and it is a great month. It was called the Deaf because no month approaches it in sanctity and virtue before Allah, Blessed and Exalted. The people of the Age of Ignorance used to revere it in their ignorance, and when Islam came it only increased in reverence and virtue. Indeed, Rajab and Sha'ban are my two months, and the month of Ramadan is the month of my community. Whoever fasts a day of Rajab out of faith and seeking reward becomes entitled to the greatest pleasure of Allah, and his fasting on that day extinguishes the wrath of Allah, and a gate of the gates of the Fire is closed for him. Even if he were given the fill of the earth in gold, it would not be better than his fasting, and his reward cannot be completed with anything of this world short of good deeds, if he makes it sincere for Allah, Mighty and Glorious. He will have ten answered supplications at evening time.",
      "And whoever fasts two days of Rajab, no tongue can describe and no mind can comprehend his status before Allah. And whoever fasts three days, Allah places between him and the Fire a trench or a barrier whose distance is like the distance of seventy years of travel. Whoever fasts seven days, the seven gates of Hell are closed for him. Whoever fasts eight days, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him. Whoever fasts ten days, Allah transforms his sins into good deeds. Whoever fasts fifteen days, a caller calls from heaven: Allah has forgiven what has passed. So begin a new account. And whoever increases, Allah increases for him.",
      "And whoever fasts twenty days of Rajab, it is as if he fasted twenty thousand years. And whoever fasts twenty-one days, on the Day of Resurrection he will see a palace of rubies. Whoever fasts twenty-two days, a caller calls: Glad tidings for you of a paradise whose width encompasses the heavens and the earth. And whoever fasts twenty-five days of Rajab, forty thousand angels greet him on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever fasts twenty-seven days, Allah expands his grave forty years of light. And whoever fasts twenty-nine days, Allah forgives him even if he were a tax-collector.",
      "And whoever fasts the full thirty days of Rajab, a caller from heaven calls: O servant of Allah, what has passed has been forgiven, so begin your deeds anew. And Allah gives him forty palaces in Paradise, each palace having a thousand rooms and in each room a thousand angels. And he is given the reward of a thousand martyrs and a thousand truthful ones. His light shines like the sun on the Day of Resurrection. He is among those whom Allah has drawn near. The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was asked: How can a servant attain what you have described? He said: He glorifies Allah, Mighty and Glorious, every day of Rajab until the completion of thirty days with this glorification one hundred times: Glory be to the Majestic God. Glory be to the One for whom glorification befits none other. Glory be to the Most Mighty, the Most Generous. Glory be to the One who has donned might and is worthy of it."
    ],
    "key_terms": {
      "رجب الأصم": "Rajab the Deaf — the sacred month so called because no month approaches it in sanctity",
      "رضوان الله الأكبر": "The Greatest Pleasure of Allah — the supreme reward for fasting in Rajab",
      "سبحان الإله الجليل": "Glory be to the Majestic God — opening of the special Rajab tasbih"
    },
    "seo_question": "What are the rewards of fasting in the month of Rajab according to the Prophet Muhammad?",
    "summary": "This lengthy hadith from the Prophet Muhammad (SAWA), transmitted through Imam al-Sadiq and narrated by Abu Said al-Khudri, describes the immense spiritual rewards for fasting during the month of Rajab. The Prophet explains that Rajab is the Deaf month of Allah — so named because no month approaches it in sanctity. He then enumerates the rewards for fasting one day, two days, three days, and so on up to thirty days, each with escalating rewards including forgiveness of sins, palaces in Paradise, intercession of angels, and light in the grave. The hadith concludes with a specific glorification (tasbih) to be recited one hundred times daily throughout Rajab to attain these rewards.",
